{
  "an1.268:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 1.268–277 ",
  "an1.268:0.2": "Chapter One ",
  "an1.268:1.0": "268 ",
  "an1.268:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual accomplished in view to take any condition as permanent. That is not possible. ",
  "an1.268:1.2": "But it is possible for an ordinary person to take some condition as permanent. That is possible.” ",
  "an1.269:1.0": "269 ",
  "an1.269:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual accomplished in view to take any condition as pleasant. ",
  "an1.269:1.2": "But it is possible for an ordinary person to take some condition as pleasant.” ",
  "an1.270:1.0": "270 ",
  "an1.270:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual accomplished in view to take anything as self. ",
  "an1.270:1.2": "But it is possible for an ordinary person to take something as self.” ",
  "an1.271:1.0": "271 ",
  "an1.271:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual accomplished in view to murder their mother. ",
  "an1.271:1.2": "But it is possible for an ordinary person to murder their mother.” ",
  "an1.272:1.0": "272 ",
  "an1.272:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual accomplished in view to murder their father. ",
  "an1.272:1.2": "But it is possible for an ordinary person to murder their father.” ",
  "an1.273:1.0": "273 ",
  "an1.273:1.1": "“It is impossible, mendicants, it cannot happen for an individual